        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Who is an agent for the platform, how does it get a token, and how does it act on behalf of a user?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: Keycloak realm 3istor with one client per hosted agent and standard token exchange (Keycloak 26.2+), proposal of 2026-10-25 · drawn in full: what the proposal adds (IA-1, IA-2) · faded: what already runs&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: how the gateway uses the claims (AI gateway internals) · OPA rules on claims (IA-3) · SPIFFE workload identity, a later option&lt;br&gt;Assumed: the CMP provisions agent clients through the Admin API; secrets go through Vault and VSO; no mTLS-bound tokens (CVE-2026-97846 affects exchange with them)&lt;br&gt;v0.2 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp · keycloak.org (token exchange, 26.2 announcement)&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
